rs of plant growth and development</article-title><source>Annual Review of Plant Physiology and Plant Molecular Biology</source><year>1998</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>451</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahl</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Meskiene</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000f6;gre</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ha</surname><given-names>DTC</given-names></name><name><surname>Swoboda</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Hubmann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirt</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Heberle-Bors</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The D-type alfalfa cyclin gene cycMs4 complements G<sub>1</sub> cyclin-deficient yeast and is induced in the G<sub>1</sub> phase of the cell cycle</article-title><source>The Plant Cell</source><year>1995</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>1847</fpage><lpage>1857</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8535138</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dhaubhadel</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaudhary</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dobinson</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Krishna</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treatment with 24-epibrassinolide, a brassinosteroid, increases the basic thermotolerance of <italic>Brassica napus</italic> and tomato seedlings</article-title><source>Plant Molecular Biology</source><year>1999</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>342</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10412911</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person